Container images
----------------

The images built from this repository (synapse, element-web and
caddy-l4) contain the upstream programs above and other third-party
software, each under its own license. The Caddy and yq binaries are
statically linked Go programs that include Go modules by other authors;
`go version -m <binary>` lists them. Every image carries this NOTICE
and LICENSE in /usr/share/licenses/siwx-oidc-matrix-server/, and:

    synapse       /usr/share/licenses/yq/LICENSE. Its Debian base lists
                  its packages' licenses in /usr/share/doc/*/copyright.
    element-web   /usr/share/licenses/element-web/ (Element Web's
                  LICENSE-AGPL-3.0 and LICENSE-GPL-3.0, from the upstream
                  checkout) and /usr/share/licenses/alpine/.
    caddy-l4      /usr/share/licenses/alpine/.

Corresponding source. The source of an image is the upstream release its
Dockerfile pins plus this repository's patches/, dockerfiles/ and the
other files the Dockerfile copies, at the commit that the image's
org.opencontainers.image.revision label names:
https://github.com/inblockio/siwx-oidc-matrix-server/tree/<revision>.

Alpine packages. The element-web image is built on
nginxinc/nginx-unprivileged:1.31.6-alpine-slim, which is Alpine Linux
3.24.2, and the caddy-l4 image on caddy:2.11.4, which is Alpine Linux
3.23.6. Their Alpine packages, BusyBox (GPL-2.0-only) among them, are
built from the aports repository; the release tags and source archives
are:

    Alpine Linux 3.24.2
        https://gitlab.alpinelinux.org/alpine/aports/-/tree/v3.24.2
        https://distfiles.alpinelinux.org/distfiles/v3.24/
    Alpine Linux 3.23.6
        https://gitlab.alpinelinux.org/alpine/aports/-/tree/v3.23.6
        https://distfiles.alpinelinux.org/distfiles/v3.23/

Each package's aports origin and commit are recorded in the image's
/lib/apk/db/installed (fields o: and c:). The texts of the licenses these
packages declare are in /usr/share/licenses/alpine/, taken from SPDX
license-list-data v3.29.0. The nginx package in the element-web image is
NGINX's own build (https://github.com/nginx/pkg-oss), not an aports
package; its license is in /usr/share/licenses/nginx/COPYRIGHT. tzdata and
mailcap declare themselves public domain and have no license text.
